NAME
    useradd - add a new user account

SYNOPSIS
    useradd NAME

DESCRIPTION
    Root-only. Adds a user called NAME (lowercase letters,
    digits, '_' and '-' only) to /etc/passwd, prompting for a
    password twice. The new user gets uid >= 1000, primary group
    users (100), a home directory /home/NAME, owned by them with
    mode 0700.

SEE ALSO
    man passwd, man su
